  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chefland consists of nnn cities numbered 111, 222, …n\\ldots n…n. The cities numbered 111, 222, …k\\ldots k…k are special cities. For each unordered pair i,ji, ji,j, there exists a bidirectional road, destroying which has a cost of wi,jw_{i, j}wi,j​. Find the minimum cost of destroying some subset of roads so that no two special cities have a path between them after the removal of these roads.\n\n\nInput Format\nThere are multiple independent testcases.\n\n\n\nFirst line will contain TTT, number of testcases.\nThe first line of each testcase contains nnn and kkk, the number of cities and the number of special cities respectively.\nThe jthj^{\\text{th}}jth integer in ithi^{\\text{th}}ith of the next nnn lines is wijw_{ij}wij​.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each testcase, output the minimum cost of destroying some subset of roads so that no two special cities have a path between them after the removal of these roads.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤51 \\leq T \\leq 51≤T≤5",
      "3≤n≤203 \\leq n \\leq 203≤n≤20",
      "3≤k≤n3 \\leq k \\leq n3≤k≤n",
      "The sum of nnn over all testcases doesn't exceed 202020.",
      "For all iii, wii=0w_{ii} = 0wii​=0",
      "For all i≠ji \\neq ji=j, wij=wjiw_{ij} = w_{ji}wij​=wji​, 1≤wij≤1061 \\leq w_{ij} \\leq 10^61≤wij​≤106"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "1\n4 3\n0 1 4 2\n1 0 2 2\n4 2 0 3\n2 2 3 0",
        "output": "11",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nRemove the roads (1,2)(1, 2)(1,2), (1,3)(1, 3)(1,3), (1,4)(1, 4)(1,4), (2,3)(2, 3)(2,3), (2,4)(2, 4)(2,4) to get a cost of 1+4+2+2+2=111 + 4 + 2 + 2 + 2 = 111+4+2+2+2=11."
      }
    ]
